  dump, under that name or any other: anything else is refused, with a
  message naming the file it wants.

-- WHAT IT DOES --------------------------------------------------------------
  Moving figures become Next hardware sprites, so they keep their own colours
  and no longer take on the scenery's (colour clash). Game logic is unchanged.

  Colours     Default (the game's own) plus: Enhanced, chosen on the menu, off
              by default.
  Enhanced    All 34 pictures painted with 12 fixed colours: Charlie in ivory
              with peach skin and a coral neckerchief, the ingredients in
              butter yellow, caramel and cornflower, the nasties in mint and
              emerald; a pixel left unpainted keeps the game's colour. A first
              pass. Off by default. A painted set, colourist not named.

  Pace        original

  Changes     1.0: figures as hardware sprites in their own colours over the
              game's own drawing
              1.1: Enhanced colours (painted, a first pass), two cheats, and
              the Next's DivMMC automap switched off at the start: NextZXOS
              leaves it on, and on current cores that could crash the game or
              spoil its drawing

  Note        Charlie, his flour bombs, the ingredients and the nasties are
              hardware sprites in their own colours, laid on the pixels the
              game still draws, so one figure no longer colours another as
              they cross. Enhanced paints the sprites. Proven on machine-
              played games and on every graphic through the game's own draw
              routine; later levels are not proven in play. Pace: kept by
              design, the same method as Jet Pac 1.3; not measured for this
              game.

-- MENU ----------------------------------------------------------------------
   1  Infinite lives
   2  Immunity

  From an archive .pok for this game, each checked against this dump by
  reading the code it changes. Infinite lives also tested in machine play: the
  lives count never falls. Immunity is not played.

